<h2>Quick workflow</h2><table><tr><th>Step</th><th>Action</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Open <b>attendance_import_template.xlsx</b>. Keep the header names unchanged.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Enter one employee shift per row. Use the built-in dropdowns for status and attendance type.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Upload from Attendance → Manual Entry → Excel Import.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Review CREATED, UPDATED, UNCHANGED, and ERROR results for every row. Correct only failed rows and upload again.</td></tr></table>
<div class="box"><b>Employee matching:</b> Always use the exact Employee ID from the Employees page, for example <b>EMP001</b> or <b>FS-000013</b>. Names are not used because they can be duplicated.</div>
