<div class="page"></div><h2>Attendance types and GPS behavior</h2><table><tr><th>Type</th><th>Use</th><th>Verification</th></tr><tr><td><b>MANUAL</b></td><td>Paper register, supervisor entry, or office-prepared attendance.</td><td>Coordinates are ignored; record is marked as manually verified.</td></tr><tr><td><b>GPS</b></td><td>Imported device/GPS data.</td><td>Clock-in coordinates are required and checked against the scheduled site's GPS radius.</td></tr><tr><td><b>MIXED</b></td><td>Manual record with optional GPS evidence.</td><td>When coordinates exist they are checked against the site; otherwise the record remains a manual decision.</td></tr></table>
<h2>Status rules</h2><table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td>PRESENT</td><td>Attended normally.</td></tr><tr><td>LATE</td><td>Late without permission.</td></tr><tr><td>LATE_WITH_PERMISSION</td><td>Late with approved permission.</td></tr><tr><td>ABSENT</td><td>Absent without permission; times and GPS are not required.</td></tr><tr><td>ABSENT_WITH_PERMISSION</td><td>Approved absence.</td></tr><tr><td>POLICY_VIOLATION</td><td>Attended but violated a rule, such as uniform requirements. A note is mandatory.</td></tr></table>
<h2>Duplicates and safe updates</h2><div class="box"><b>UNCHANGED:</b> An attendance record already exists and every imported value is the same.<br><b>UPDATED:</b> A record exists but one or more spreadsheet values changed; only that attendance record is updated.<br><b>CREATED:</b> No attendance exists for the matched shift.<br><b>ERROR:</b> The row is rejected and rolled back. Other rows continue.</div>
<h2>Common errors</h2><table><tr><th>Message</th><th>How to fix it</th></tr><tr><td>Employee ID was not found</td><td>Copy the exact employee code from Employees.</td></tr><tr><td>No scheduled shift found</td><td>Create the roster shift first, or correct the date/site/schedule ID.</td></tr><tr><td>Multiple shifts found</td><td>Add site_id or schedule_id.</td></tr><tr><td>Missing required columns</td><td>Use the standard workbook and do not rename headers.</td></tr><tr><td>GPS coordinates required/outside range</td><td>Provide valid decimal latitude and longitude for GPS rows.</td></tr></table>
<div class="warning box"><b>Important:</b> Keep the result report until all ERROR rows are corrected. Re-uploading is safe: unchanged records are not duplicated.</div></body></html>
